    {
      "index": 6,
      "id": "537845713645120960_77767",
      "question": "\" The Census Act of 1800 was passed two years after the publication of this man's most noted book, in which he claimed agricultural production would not keep up with another metric.\nFor the point, what 18th and 19th century economist predicted catastrophic population growth in his book, An Essay on the Principle of Population?",
